{"chunk_id": "a20e62488408", "text": "Markandeya recounts the chain of events that leads to Sita\u2019s abduction. After Rama defeats the Rakshasas of Janasthana, the humiliated Surpanakha informs Ravana, who seeks out the Rakshasa Maricha. Maricha warns Ravana that provoking Rama will bring destruction, recalling Rama\u2019s terrifying prowess, but Ravana threatens him with death unless he helps. Resigned, Maricha agrees to assist in a deception: he will transform into a golden deer to lure Rama away while Ravana abducts Sita. The plan unfolds at Rama\u2019s forest hermitage. Enchanted by the deer, Sita asks Rama to capture it; Rama pursues and eventually kills the disguised Maricha. With his dying breath Maricha imitates Rama\u2019s voice calling for help, prompting Sita\u2014fearful and desperate\u2014to send Lakshmana after him, leaving her vulnerable to Ravana\u2019s scheme.\nRavana recruits Maricha to lure Rama away with a golden deer so he can abduct Sita, despite Maricha\u2019s warning about Rama\u2019s power.\nThemes: deception and disguise, fate and inevitability, loyalty and coercion, abduction plot, warning ignored", "vector": [-0.004113775212317705, -0.015387815423309803, 0.0028573512099683285, -0.0121859610080719, -0.02969483658671379, 0.012449405156075954, -0.042691394686698914, -0.017130596563220024, -0.02530410885810852, -0.016617219895124435, 0.016401061788201332, 0.01353695522993803, -0.0009254305623471737, 0.020670199766755104, -0.007018411066383123, -0.0013062418438494205, 0.039692189544439316, -0.009814967401325703, 0.021386226639151573, -0.02443947270512581, -0.007606093306094408, 0.0013526822440326214, -0.004427880980074406, 0.0100581469014287, -0.030910730361938477, 0.010085166431963444, 0.020008213818073273, -0.02837086282670498, 0.009936557151377201, -0.014144902117550373, -0.008207285776734352, -0.02589854598045349, 0.002894503530114889, -0.0219536442309618, -0.022885829210281372, -0.006684040185064077, 0.016022782772779465, -0.0141449021